# Keeps the Docker build context (repo root) small and avoids ever baking secrets or
# repo-local files into an image. infra/docker/*.Dockerfile COPY the whole repo root into their
# `pruner` stage, then use `turbo prune`, so this only needs to exclude what turbo prune doesn't
# already narrow down for us, plus anything that must never reach a build context at all.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.turbo
**/.turbo
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
coverage
**/coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets: never send a real .env file to the Docker daemon, even accidentally. .env.example
# files are fine (and needed by nothing at build time, but harmless either way).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Docs are not read by any app at build or run time (docs/openapi/README.md documents that
# docs/openapi/ itself is only touched by the `openapi:generate`/`openapi:check` CLI scripts,
# which run outside Docker) — excluding the whole tree keeps the build context small.
docs

.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
